    narr:narration """A cutover-planning call opened by [Tanya framing the stakes around a Thursday steering-group deadline](narr:Expr_1HalyardWeekly20260908_1), with [Xavier holding replica numbers in reserve](narr:Expr_1HalyardWeekly20260908_3) while [Tina laid out the four sites, flagging the one nobody wants to touch](narr:Expr_1HalyardWeekly20260908_5). Tanya [stated her position firmly: one site at a time, no parallel cutovers](narr:Expr_1HalyardWeekly20260908_8), which [Xavier stress-tested by raising the shared dispatch desk](narr:Expr_1HalyardWeekly20260908_12); she [answered with the contained-versus-unbounded trade](narr:Expr_1HalyardWeekly20260908_13), and [Tina backed it with the rota-versus-staffing distinction](narr:Expr_1HalyardWeekly20260908_15). [Tina then put a number on the soak](narr:Expr_1HalyardWeekly20260908_17), [grounding it in the Dockside exception curve](narr:Expr_1HalyardWeekly20260908_19), which [Xavier noted rests on a single site and season](narr:Expr_1HalyardWeekly20260908_21) — [Tina accepted the caveat and held the line anyway](narr:Expr_1HalyardWeekly20260908_22). Xavier then [argued reporting reads must come off the replica during cutover](narr:Expr_1HalyardWeekly20260908_26), [pricing the cost as replica lag against an outage](narr:Expr_1HalyardWeekly20260908_28), and [Tanya made it a runbook rule, not guidance](narr:Expr_1HalyardWeekly20260908_31). Finally, [Xavier proposed the vendor stays system of record for reference data until the last site is live](narr:Expr_1HalyardWeekly20260908_36), [reasoning from zone-map drift](narr:Expr_1HalyardWeekly20260908_38), with [Tanya adding the vendor-blame shield](narr:Expr_1HalyardWeekly20260908_39). The call closed with [Tanya reciting the four decisions back for confirmation](narr:Expr_1HalyardWeekly20260908_42).""" ;
